## The magistrates
Matters you cannot settle yourself — a theft, a debt in dispute, a wrong one villager lays at another's door — go before the magistrates in Salem Town. They sit each day at noon, read what passed in the village, and send word of their ruling to everyone the matter concerns; their ruling ends it. You have brought 2 matters today; the court hears no more from you until tomorrow.
Before the court now, as you brought it: "Joseph Scott's account book was taken from the Mill some days past; no one will say who took it." (Joseph Scott, Constable Gideon Marsh) — the court has sat, and its word has not yet come.
Weigh what's in front of you — obligations and pressing needs come before idle matters. Choose one action, then call done() when nothing pressing remains.
